# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root .dockerignore - Docker Image Optimization Skill (§6)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API and Engine Dockerfiles use the repo root as build context
# (see docker-compose.build.yml). This file keeps the build context
# small and deterministic: only the files those Dockerfiles actually
# COPY are ever sent to the Docker daemon.
# (Frontend builds use ./frontend as context and have their own
#  .dockerignore.)

# VCS / CI / repo metadata
.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.gitmodules

# Node.js
node_modules
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Build outputs & caches
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.cache
.parcel-cache
.turbo
.vercel

# Environment & secrets (never send to the Docker daemon)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.mcp.json

# Packages / directories not referenced by the API/Engine images
frontend
sdks
docs
scripts
sql
# supabase/migrations IS needed in the API image: the entrypoint auto-migrates
# from MIGRATIONS_DIR (/app/backend/migrations), and until now that directory
# only ever existed as a docker-compose bind mount. Any host that ran the image
# without the mount - Railway being the one in production - skipped
# auto-migration entirely, which is how a database full of stale webhook
# ownership FKs survived every redeploy. Excluding the rest of supabase/ keeps
# the context small (config.toml, functions, seed files are not needed).
supabase/*
!supabase/migrations
!supabase/migrations/**
caddy
nginx
load-tests

# Repo-level files not needed inside images
*.md
install.sh
uninstall.sh
update.sh
renovate.json
LICENSE
TRADEMARK.md

# Model weights downloaded by engine/download-models.js at build time -
# never needed in the build context (the image downloads its own copy)
engine/models

# Logs, temp, uploads, IDE & OS noise
logs
**/logs
**/tmp
**/temp
**/uploads
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.agents
.aidesigner
